# Commit and push after changes

After completing and verifying any change in this project, create a focused Git commit and push the current branch to its configured remote.

- Include only files changed for the current request; do not include unrelated working-tree changes.
- Run relevant verification before committing when practical.
- Report the commit hash and push result to the user.
